        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: బుట్ట",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "బుట్ట (buṭṭa) — \"a basket\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "బుట్ట (buṭṭa) is inherited: the woven basket that carries vegetables home, holds flowers for the morning, and sits on a head on the way to market."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Weaving words tend to be old, and they tend to stay put while the trade words move around them. A బుట్ట (buṭṭa) and a చాప (cāpa) come off the same hands and the same palm leaf, which is why the two words feel like family even though they are not."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పూల బుట్ట (buṭṭa) is the flower basket — పువ్వు's పూల- shape doing its work again."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two: something to sit on, something to carry with."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
