        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: కత్తి",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కత్తి (katti) — \"a knife\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కత్తి (katti) is the knife and, in older use, the sword. Size did not divide them; the blade did."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is inherited, and it is spread right across the family — Tamil, Kannada and Malayalam all have a word of the same shape for a cutting blade. Tools that a household could make for itself keep their names for a very long time."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కత్తి (katti) also does the work English gives to \"sharp\" when talking about people: కత్తిలాంటి is knife-like, said of somebody quick."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
