        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: గిన్నె",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "గిన్నె (ginne) — \"a cooking vessel, a bowl\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "గిన్నె (ginne) is the round metal vessel that food is cooked and served in — the everyday one, brass or steel, with no lid worth mentioning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Telugu splits its containers finely. A గిన్నె (ginne) is not a కుండ, the fired clay pot, and it is not a పళ్ళెం, the flat plate. English pushes all three towards \"pot\" and \"dish\" and loses the difference between what holds heat, what holds water and what holds a meal."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "When a kitchen has a name for each shape, the names are telling you which shapes the kitchen actually uses."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four."
            }
          ]
        },
